# Build context exclusions for both deployables (Dockerfile, Dockerfile.inference).
#
# Without this file the context is the whole working tree — `target/` alone is
# multiple gigabytes on any machine that has run `cargo build`, and every
# `make quickstart` / `docker compose build` uploads all of it to the daemon
# before the first layer is even considered.
#
# Deliberately a denylist, not an allowlist (`*` + `!` re-includes): a new
# `COPY` in either Dockerfile keeps working by default here, whereas under an
# allowlist it would fail at build time with a missing path. Everything named
# below is either a build artifact, a local secret, or something no `COPY` in
# either Dockerfile reads.
#
# NOTE ON SYNTAX: this is not .gitignore. Docker matches with Go's
# `filepath.Match` against the whole context-relative path, so a bare
# `__pycache__` matches ONLY at the context root — it does not apply at every
# depth the way the same line does in .gitignore. Anything that must match at
# any depth needs an explicit `**/` prefix, which is why the recursive block
# below is spelled that way.

# Compiled output. The single biggest entry, and never an input: both images
# build from source in their own builder stage.
target

# Not a build input, and it carries the full history.
.git
.gitignore

# Local docker-compose overrides. `make ensure-inference-token` writes a real
# ARMOR_INFERENCE_AUTH_TOKEN here, so this must never reach the daemon or a
# build cache. No COPY reads it today; this keeps that true if one is added.
.env

# Bind-mount target for model weights (gigabytes, pinned by digest — see
# .gitignore). The image never contains weights; the sidecar fetches them.
models

# Operator-authored config. The images ship the tracked defaults
# (config/policies.yaml, config/ml_catalog.yaml); these are deployment-specific
# and can carry identifiers that should not be baked into an image. The
# `.yaml.example` templates do not match these patterns and stay in context.
config/applications.yaml
config/profiles/*.yaml
config/custom_rules/*.yaml

# Python build and test artifacts, at any depth. `inference/src` is COPYied
# wholesale by Dockerfile.inference, so without the `**/` these would ride
# along into the image — stale bytecode from a different interpreter version
# is the failure mode.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
inference/build
inference/dist
inference/.venv

# Not read by any COPY in either Dockerfile.
docs
scripts
.github
integrations
**/*.log
**/*.old
